\code{NA}), \code{EF_GWR_EXTRAPOLATION_COVARIATE} (1; GWR and OLS),
\code{EF_GWR_EXTRAPOLATION_LOCAL} (2; GWR with compact kernels),
\code{EF_GWR_OUTSIDE_HULL} (3; GWR, OLS, IDW), \code{EF_GWR_FEW_NEIGHBOURS} (4) and
\code{EF_GWR_LOCAL_SINGULAR} (5; GWR), and \code{EF_GWR_OUT_OF_DOMAIN} (6, class
III, \code{critical}): the prediction is outside the physical domain of the
variable (air temperature <= -273.15 degC, vapour pressure <= 0, wind
speed, clearness, solar radiation or daily reference ET < 0,
instantaneous reference ET <= 0). Out-of-domain values are \strong{kept} and
flagged, never truncated; their consumers reject them with
\code{earthflux_domain_error}. Counts per layer and code are in
\code{provenance$flags$counts}. Object scope: \code{EF_GWR_SINGLE_STATION} (C1),
