\section{Parallel processing}{

Sequential by default. If the user has set a \code{future} plan with more than
one worker (e.g. \code{future::plan(future::multisession, workers = 2)}), the
fits (one per target time) and the prediction blocks are evaluated with
\code{future.apply::future_lapply()} (\code{future.seed = TRUE}); EarthFlux never
sets a plan nor changes \code{terra} or R options. The results are identical
for any plan, number of workers and block size; the plan used is recorded
in \code{provenance$execution}. A \code{SpatRaster} keeps a pointer to \code{terra}
memory: save the result with \code{filename} or \code{terra::wrap()}, not with
\code{saveRDS()} alone.
}

